.TH SOS\-DESKTOP 1 "2026-06-06" "sos-desktop 0.1.0" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
sos\-desktop \- desktop front\-end for the sos suite of diagnostic tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sos\-desktop
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sos\-desktop
is a graphical (PyQt6) front\-end for the
.BR sos (1)
suite of diagnostic tools.
It provides a point\-and\-click interface for the most common sos workflows:
generating a report on the local system, uploading an archive to a support
portal, collecting reports from multiple nodes simultaneously, and obfuscating
sensitive data from an existing archive.
.PP
No sos subcommand is ever run as root.
Individual commands that require elevated privileges are wrapped with
.BR pkexec (1)
so that the user is prompted for credentials by the system's polkit agent.
.SH INTERFACE
The window is divided into three areas.
.TP
.B Top bar
Persistent settings that apply to all commands: Case ID, upload target,
and verbose mode.
These values are saved between sessions using
.BR QSettings .
.TP
.B Sidebar
Action buttons, one per sos operation.
Clicking a button launches the corresponding command and streams its output
to the output panel.
.TP
.B Output panel
Displays live subprocess output.
A progress bar appears while a command is running.
The status label below the output shows the result when the command finishes.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B Generate Report
Runs
.B sos report \-\-batch
elevated via
.BR pkexec .
The resulting archive is written to
.IR /var/tmp .
.TP
.B Upload Selected
Runs
.B sos upload
on the archive selected in the SOS Reports table.
Optionally passes
.BI \-\-upload\-target " TARGET"
and
.BI \-\-case\-id " ID"
when those fields are set in the top bar.
.TP
.B Generate Remote Report
Runs
.B sos report
on a remote host over SSH.
Prompts for the remote hostname, SSH user, SSH key, and port before
launching.
.TP
.B Multi\-node Collect
Opens a configuration dialog (nodes, cluster type, transport, SSH options,
parallelism) and then runs
.B sos collect
with the resulting options.
.TP
.B Obfuscate Report
Runs
.B sos clean
elevated via
.BR pkexec
on the archive selected in the SOS Reports table.
Prompts for any additional keywords to obfuscate before launching.
Replaces IP addresses, MAC addresses, hostnames, and custom keywords
throughout the archive.
.TP
.B Authorize System
Runs
.B sos upload \-\-preauth \-\-batch
to store an upload auth token without sending a file.
This requires a version of
.BR sos (1)
that supports the
.B \-\-preauth
flag.
If the installed sos does not support
.BR \-\-preauth ,
a warning is shown and the command is not run.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/tmp/sosreport\-*.tar.xz
Default location for sos report archives.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sos\-desktop/sos\-desktop.conf
QSettings configuration file (location may vary by desktop environment).
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.TP
.B sos
The
.BR sos (1)
package must be installed and in
.IR PATH .
.TP
.B pkexec + polkit agent
Required for commands that need root privileges.
A graphical polkit agent must be running in the session.
.TP
.B xdg\-open or gio
Used to open files and folders from the reports table.
.TP
.B ssh
Required only for the Generate Remote Report action.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B sos\-desktop
itself always exits 0.
Exit codes from underlying sos commands are shown in the output panel and
status label.
.PP
.BR pkexec (1)
exit codes have the following meaning:
.TP
.B 126
The user dismissed or failed the polkit authentication prompt.
No action is taken.
.TP
.B 127
The action was denied by polkit policy.
A warning dialog is shown.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sos (1),
.BR sos\-report (1),
.BR sos\-upload (1),
.BR sos\-collect (1),
.BR sos\-clean (1),
.BR pkexec (1)
